@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1384 = private unnamed_addr constant [25 x i8] c"docstring-tab-indentation", align 1
@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1385 = private unnamed_addr constant [1244 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for docstrings that are indented with tabs.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 8] recommends using spaces over tabs for indentation.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef sort_list(l: list[int]) -> list[int]:\0A    \22\22\22Return a sorted copy of the list.\0A\0A\09Sort the list in ascending order and return a copy of the result using the bubble\0A\09sort algorithm.\0A    \22\22\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef sort_list(l: list[int]) -> list[int]:\0A    \22\22\22Return a sorted copy of the list.\0A\0A    Sort the list in ascending order and return a copy of the result using the bubble\0A    sort algorithm.\0A    \22\22\22\0A```\0A\0A## Formatter compatibility\0AWe recommend against using this rule alongside the [formatter]. The\0Aformatter enforces consistent indentation, making the rule redundant.\0A\0AThe rule is also incompatible with the [formatter] when using\0A`format.indent-style=\22tab\22`.\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A- [NumPy Style Guide](https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html)\0A- [Google Python Style Guide - Docstrings](https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#38-comments-and-docstrings)\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#tabs-or-spaces\0A[formatter]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter\0A", align 1
