@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1499 = private unnamed_addr constant [689 x i8] c"## Removed\0AThis rule is identical to [S307] which should be used instead.\0A\0A## What it does\0AChecks for uses of the builtin `eval()` function.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `eval()` function is insecure as it enables arbitrary code execution.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef foo():\0A    x = eval(input(\22Enter a number: \22))\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef foo():\0A    x = input(\22Enter a number: \22)\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `eval`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#eval)\0A- [_Eval really is dangerous_ by Ned Batchelder](https://nedbatchelder.com/blog/201206/eval_really_is_dangerous.html)\0A\0A[S307]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/suspicious-eval-usage/\0A", align 1
