@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1533 = private unnamed_addr constant [711 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of names that are declared as `global` prior to the\0Arelevant `global` declaration.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `global` declaration applies to the entire scope. Using a name that's\0Adeclared as `global` in a given scope prior to the relevant `global`\0Adeclaration is a `SyntaxError`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Acounter = 1\0A\0A\0Adef increment():\0A    print(f\22Adding 1 to {counter}\22)\0A    global counter\0A    counter += 1\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Acounter = 1\0A\0A\0Adef increment():\0A    global counter\0A    print(f\22Adding 1 to {counter}\22)\0A    counter += 1\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: The `global` statement](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/simple_stmts.html#the-global-statement)\0A", align 1
