@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1565 = private unnamed_addr constant [602 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `bin(...)[2:]` (or `hex`, or `oct`) to convert\0Aan integer into a string.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhen converting an integer to a baseless binary, hexadecimal, or octal\0Astring, using f-strings is more concise and readable than using the\0A`bin`, `hex`, or `oct` functions followed by a slice.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aprint(bin(1337)[2:])\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aprint(f\22{1337:b}\22)\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThe fix is only marked as safe for integer literals, all other cases\0Aare display-only, as they may change the runtime behaviour of the program\0Aor introduce syntax errors.\0A", align 1
